  "notes": "Bubblegum teen-pop with Swedish-style production imported to Orlando and New York: 95–115 straight, backbeat on 2&4, bright G major with I–vi–IV–V and I–V–vi–IV loops and no modulation. Three drum facts are stated and all three are authored — \"clap on 2&4 stacked with snare\" (the clap offset widened), \"16th hat pattern with an open hat on the last 8th of the bar\" (a pinned 16th base with the open hat on \"4&\" every bar), and \"'twinkling' bell/glockenspiel figures used as percussion\", which is why a triangle lane leads the percs. The bass is \"root-and-fifth 8ths locked to the kick\", so `mirror_kick` at 0.94 with the fifth as its only passing tone, and the melody is \"in a 1-octave span, chorus hook a repeated 2-bar cell with a call-and-response backing stack\" — a narrow register, a two-bar phrase weighting and a `call_response` structure. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research says the tempo band is **[LOW-CONF]**, \"inferred from the bubblegum-pop convention, not a per-song reading\"; `bpm.mode` 104 is this author's centre of that band. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and the counter numbers.",
